;; Drives temperature.clj for docs/demos/temperature.gif.
;;
;; The two-step shape is the point: :tap-by-role focuses the field through the
;; accessibility API, and only THEN does a synthetic :type land in it. Typing
;; without focusing first goes to whatever app is frontmost — which is why an
;; earlier probe here concluded, wrongly, that synthetic input cannot reach an
;; AppKit window at all.
;;
;; command+a before typing because the field already holds "0"; without it the
;; text appends and the field reads "0100".
[[:wait-for-quiescence 600]
 [:tap-by-role {:role "AXTextField" :text "0"}]
 [:wait-for-quiescence 400]
 [:key "command + a"]
 [:type "100"]
 [:wait-for-quiescence 1200]
 [:key "command + a"]
 [:type "37"]
 [:wait-for-quiescence 1200]]
